# The machine's own settings for zero-core and the game repos (mtg-zero, ...). Copy this file to
# ~/.config/zero/local.env (or point $ZERO_LOCAL_CONFIG at another file) and fill in what this
# machine has. That file is never committed: the repositories are public, so ssh targets, host
# names, IP addresses and home-directory paths live only there (AGENTS.md "Private details").
# KEY=value lines; '#' comments; quote a value with spaces. An environment variable of the same
# name wins over the file. Every key is optional: unset = the generic default.

# A big scratch disk for build dirs, smoke runs and scratch (Windows desktops with a small C:).
# Unset: each checkout's own target/ and the system's temp directory.
#ZERO_BIG_DISK=E:

# mtg-zero: the MacBook used as a remote worker and for the gate's offload (tools/mac.sh,
# eval_remote / selfplay_remote 'mac'). Unset: no Mac (the gate runs everything locally).
#MTGZ_MAC=user@mac-host
#MTGZ_MAC_HOME=/Users/user

# zerodash: its projects file (default ~/.config/zero/projects.json; dashboard/projects.example.json).
#ZERODASH_CONFIG=/path/to/projects.json

# tools/privacy_check.py: extra patterns that must never appear in a tracked file (the real names of
# this machine's hosts, farm machines, accounts): one regex per line in
# ~/.config/zero/privacy_patterns.txt (or $ZERO_PRIVACY_PATTERNS). See tools/privacy_patterns.example.txt.
